8883
00:09:29,710 --> 00:09:33,030
If it looks like a fight's about to 
break out, come straight back here.

8884
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:36,020
Our goal is not to fight.

8885
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:38,220
It's to find out if our 
nations can get along,

8886
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:41,320
or if we need to sever relations with them.

8887
00:09:41,810 --> 00:09:43,540
Although this is for the good of Tempest,

8888
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:46,310
you don't need to force yourself 
to endure any more than necessary.

8889
00:09:46,950 --> 00:09:47,810
I'm counting on you!

8890
00:09:47,810 --> 00:09:49,230
Yes, sir!

8891
00:09:52,230 --> 00:09:56,930
Great Rimuru! I'm so moved!

8892
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:57,740
There, there...

8893
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:04,030
I should be the one going 
out there, to be honest.

8894
00:10:04,030 --> 00:10:07,060
No, until we confirm that it is safe,

8895
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:09,710
I believe you should refrain from 
entering a Demon Lord's domain.

8896
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:14,730
I will discern with my own eyes whether or 
not the Demon Lord Carrion can be trusted.

8897
00:10:14,730 --> 00:10:15,460
Thanks.

8898
00:10:15,470 --> 00:10:18,970
Remember, whatever you do, 
don't go picking a fight.

8899
00:10:18,970 --> 00:10:20,660
No need to worry.

8900
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:24,060
So reliable! Benimaru's really grown up!

8901
00:10:24,690 --> 00:10:26,520
Good luck to you guys, too, Rigur.

8902
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:29,060
Thank you. I will gain as 
much experience as I can.

8903
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:33,070
We'll be on our way now.

8904
00:10:39,070 --> 00:10:41,670
Have fun, you guys!

8905
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:43,250
Take care!

8906
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:44,830
Good luck!

8907
00:10:44,830 --> 00:10:47,820
Be safe, Brother!

8908
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:47,820
Good luck, everyone!

8909
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:51,830
The first steps toward 
hope for our future, huh?

8910
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:54,650
Here's hoping we can establish 
formal diplomatic relations

8911
00:10:54,650 --> 00:10:58,070
and help both of our nations grow even more.

8912
00:11:00,010 --> 00:11:04,000
Thus the first delegation from 
our nation set out on its way.

8913
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:10,600
And we have to get things ready here at home 
to welcome Eurazania's delegation, too.

8914
00:11:12,610 --> 00:11:16,710
Good, good. Looks like the reception 
hall will be ready in time.

8915
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:18,610
How are the chefs doing?

8916
00:11:18,610 --> 00:11:19,110
Just fine.

8917
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,720
Princess Shuna is teaching them.

8918
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:24,550
They're all quick learners 
and coming along well.

8919
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:29,100
Yes... I think it could 
use just a bit more salt.

8920
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:32,320
As for the reception hall waiting staff,

8921
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,630
Vesta is giving them guidance.

8922
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:37,410
I guess proper etiquette 
is kind of his forte.

8923
00:11:37,410 --> 00:11:39,130
We can always count on an actual noble.

8924
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,750
And, um... also...

8925
00:11:41,750 --> 00:11:45,140
The date for your visit to the 
Armed Nation of Dwargon has been set.

8926
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:47,310
Oh, yeah. I need to see King Gazel in person

8927
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:52,140
to thank him again for establishing 
diplomatic relations with Tempest.

8928
00:11:52,150 --> 00:11:56,400
He's probably not too happy with Milim's 
involvement in the Charybdis incident,

8929
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:58,440
so I need to explain that, too.

8930
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:03,160
Treyni-san!

8931
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:07,910
Greetings, Great Rimuru.

8932
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:10,730
What brings you here? Has something happened?

8933
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:11,770
Yes.

8934
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:16,550
The delegation from the Animal Kingdom of 
Eurazania has entered the Great Forest of Jura.

8935
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:17,920
I wanted to inform you.

8936
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,460
Ah, so they're almost here.

8937
00:12:19,910 --> 00:12:23,840
They should arrive here in 
Tempest within five days.

8938
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:25,800
Thanks for letting me know!

8939
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:28,440
It was the least I could do.

8940
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:32,750
Also, it is likely that they will 
arrive before the delegation does.

8941
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:34,400
"They"?

8942
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,670
Yes, the champion's...

8943
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:44,970
It's getting dark. Let's go home.

8944
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:45,910
Okay!

8945
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:51,020
Mush, mush, mush...

8946
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,700
Mush!

8947
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:53,710
How cute!

8948
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:01,300
Don't move!

8949
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:10,700
Youm and his buddies.

8950
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:13,350
They used to be a gang of ruffians,

8951
00:13:13,350 --> 00:13:17,770
but I had them become the champions who 
defeated the Orc Lord in our place.

8952
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:19,960
Wow...

8953
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,220
If it got out that we defeated the Orc Lord,

8954
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:24,880
it would just make humans wary of us.

8955
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:26,570
Are you all right?

8956
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:28,740
Y-Yes... Thank you so much.

8957
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:32,710
Um... Thank you.

8958
00:13:32,710 --> 00:13:35,500
Better be careful. There are 
some nasty monsters around here.

8959
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:38,000
Your sword is so cool!

8960
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,110
I know, right?

8961
00:13:40,750 --> 00:13:44,890
I had it made in a nation of good monsters 
called Tempest that's just ahead.

8962
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:51,010
They're traveling around telling people 
everywhere that we're friendly monsters.

8963
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,890
And from then on...

8964
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:24,080
I continued to keep busy every day...

8965
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:40,560
right up until the day we welcomed 
the delegation from Eurazania.

8966
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:47,200
Wow, this is good.

8967
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:50,830
It really is. I've never had it before.

8968
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:53,910
Right? It's called brandy.

8969
00:14:54,470 --> 00:14:56,530
Brandy, you say?

8970
00:14:56,530 --> 00:14:59,540
I made it as a special treat 
since we have guests visiting.

8971
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,960
Oh, yeah? Guests?

8972
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,960
Yep. The Demon Lord Carrion's 
delegation is arriving tomorrow.

8973
00:15:07,510 --> 00:15:09,510
Did you do that on purpose?!

8974
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:13,000
The Demon Lord Carrion?!

8975
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,350
How the hell did that happen?!

8976
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:18,620
Well, it's a long story...

8977
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:22,100
This feels so nice.

8978
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,110
I see.

8979
00:15:29,110 --> 00:15:31,870
So it's our chance to establish 
diplomatic relations.

8980
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:33,490
I get it.

8981
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:35,910
A Demon Lord, though? Really?

8982
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:38,650
Sounds like that's gonna 
be one scary delegation.

8983
00:15:38,650 --> 00:15:42,370
I don't know about that. 
The goal isn't to fight.

8984
00:15:42,370 --> 00:15:46,590
But you sent Benimaru just in case 
the unforeseen happens, right?

8985
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:49,510
Wouldn't they have the same idea?

8986
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,970
If they do, it doesn't matter.

8987
00:15:51,970 --> 00:15:54,850
I don't want to make a wrong 
move and waste this chance.

8988
00:15:54,850 --> 00:15:56,720
Yeah, I guess not.

8989
00:15:57,930 --> 00:16:00,850
You guys better not pick any fights 
with the delegates, either.

8990
00:16:00,850 --> 00:16:06,000
Hey, c'mon, Master. 
My boys and I aren't complete morons.

8991
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:06,900
Right?

8992
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,220
You said it.

8993
00:16:09,110 --> 00:16:10,610
That's good, then.

8994
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,450
By the way, Hakurou was hoping to see you.

8995
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:14,820
The master?!

8996
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:17,620
He wanted to make sure 
you haven't gotten rusty.

8997
00:16:18,830 --> 00:16:21,040
Well, that sobered me right up.

8998
00:16:24,810 --> 00:16:27,270
Then, the next day...

8999
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:38,640
Here they come.

9000
00:16:49,350 --> 00:16:50,770
Horse-drawn carriages?

9001
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:53,820
No, those are tigers... 
Tiger-drawn carriages?

9002
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,320
They look like war chariots.

9003
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:57,210
They're no big deal.

9004
00:16:57,210 --> 00:17:01,160
In the face of your mighty power, 
that doesn't even work as a bluff.

9005
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:04,640
Wait, wait, wait, Shion-san! 
They're definitely a big deal!

9006
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:08,750
All those fancy decorations 
have no purpose in combat.

9007
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:10,170
Wait, wait, wait, Shion-san!

9008
00:17:10,170 --> 00:17:12,340
We're not talking about combat here!

9009
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:26,440
It is a pleasure to meet you,

9010
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:30,480
leader of the Jura Tempest 
Federation, Rimuru Tempest.

9011
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:35,110
I am Albis, the Golden Serpent,

9012
